      "writtenOn": "2016-05-09T22:43:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Add just a little more info for the casual reader, please. Something like: \"The idle state of the UART signals is high, so our RX will be high when the AP or EC is powered up and driving the signals. Our TX is wired directly to the servo\u0027s TX, so it will be high when servo is driving it. That\u0027s also why we shouldn\u0027t attempt to drive it when servo is.\"",
      "range": {
